{
  "id": "20803_yogen",
  "headword": "{予言|よげん}",
  "reading": "よげん",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "prediction; prophecy; forecast",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "prediction; prophecy; forecast",
      "explanation": "A statement about what will happen in the future, ranging from religious prophecy to casual predictions. Often carries a sense of authority or conviction."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "20803_yogen_ex1",
      "japanese": "その{予言|よげん}は{当|あ}たった。",
      "english": "That prediction came true.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "20803_yogen_ex2",
      "japanese": "{彼|かれ}は{未来|みらい}を{予言|よげん}した。",
      "english": "He prophesied the future.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "20803_yogen_ex3",
      "japanese": "{古代|こだい}の{予言|よげん}が{現実|げんじつ}になるとは{誰|だれ}も{思|おも}わなかった。",
      "english": "Nobody thought the ancient prophecy would come true.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Refers to foretelling future events, whether through supernatural means (prophecy) or rational analysis (prediction). The word carries more weight than a simple guess.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {予言|よげん}が{当|あ}たる: a prediction comes true\n- {予言|よげん}が{外|はず}れる: a prediction proves wrong\n- {予言|よげん}を{信|しん}じる: to believe a prophecy\n- {予言|よげん}どおり: as predicted/prophesied\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {予測|よそく}: forecast — more scientific and data-driven\n- {予想|よそう}: expectation — more informal, everyday guessing\n- {預言|よげん}: divine prophecy — specifically religious revelation (same pronunciation, different kanji)",
